WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:01.355
Glitch Academy.

00:01.355 --> 00:05.243
One student's journey, from sign-in to defeating the boss.

00:06.243 --> 00:10.222
This is Glitch Academy, a gamified web development workshop.

00:10.222 --> 00:13.935
Let's follow one student through the whole course, live.

00:16.777 --> 00:19.235
The student signs in with GitHub.

00:19.235 --> 00:23.631
Their deck shows five quests, badges and experience points.

00:23.631 --> 00:25.717
Quests unlock one at a time.

00:26.610 --> 00:32.705
On the projector, the arena shows the class as robots, facing the Glitch Overlord at full health.

00:35.610 --> 00:37.766
Learning happens in the course:

00:37.766 --> 00:43.122
five modules, each with short lessons, interactive labs, a quiz, and a quest.

00:44.877 --> 00:46.707
Module one is Git and GitHub.

00:46.707 --> 00:53.649
Here the student writes a README in a live Markdown editor, then answers a quick check to complete the lesson.

00:56.610 --> 01:00.099
Every module ends with a quiz, scored on the server.

01:00.099 --> 01:04.929
A wrong answer explains why, gives a hint, and links back to the lesson.

01:17.177 --> 01:18.918
Seventy percent passes.

01:19.843 --> 01:21.121
Now the real test.

01:21.121 --> 01:25.877
The student pushes their work to GitHub and submits the repository.

01:25.877 --> 01:27.865
The verifier checks it live:

01:27.865 --> 01:32.337
the repo is theirs, the commit is new, and the README is there.

01:35.010 --> 01:36.371
Quest one passed.

01:36.371 --> 01:39.254
A badge lights up and XP is awarded.

01:40.143 --> 01:42.262
In the arena, the hit lands.

01:42.262 --> 01:46.500
The boss loses health with every lesson, quiz and quest.

01:54.677 --> 01:58.309
Module two builds the portfolio with HTML and CSS.

01:58.309 --> 02:03.611
The glass tuner shows how a backdrop blur creates the glassmorphism look.

02:08.643 --> 02:14.959
Quiz two covers semantic HTML, the box model, flexbox and responsive design.

02:21.777 --> 02:25.417
The second commit adds a responsive portfolio page.

02:25.417 --> 02:32.127
The verifier checks the sections, the hand-written CSS, the glass effect and the viewport tag.

02:36.210 --> 02:37.290
Two badges.

02:40.210 --> 02:42.114
The Overlord is getting weaker.

02:49.743 --> 02:52.908
Module three brings 3D with Three.js.

02:52.908 --> 03:00.860
In the light lab, the scene stays pitch black until the student adds ambient light and a sun.

03:05.077 --> 03:05.899
Quiz three:

03:05.899 --> 03:09.338
scenes, meshes, lights and the animation loop.

03:17.377 --> 03:21.955
Quest three adds a rotating 3D background behind the portfolio.

03:21.955 --> 03:27.913
The verifier looks for the scene, camera, renderer, animation, and a fixed canvas.

03:33.010 --> 03:34.113
Three badges.

03:37.010 --> 03:38.322
Another direct hit.

03:46.543 --> 03:49.191
Module four loads a real 3D avatar.

03:49.191 --> 03:56.000
In Chassis Sync, the student moves, scales and turns the robot until it matches the ghost.

04:05.943 --> 04:06.923
Quiz four:

04:06.923 --> 04:12.608
model formats, the GLTF loader, file paths and transforms.

04:18.477 --> 04:24.103
For quest four, the avatar file is committed and loaded with the GLTF loader.

04:24.103 --> 04:29.803
The verifier even checks that the file path matches, capital letters included.

04:32.743 --> 04:33.777
Four badges.

04:36.743 --> 04:38.009
One quest to go.

04:46.277 --> 04:48.124
Module five builds a chatbot.

04:48.124 --> 04:55.257
In the intent router, the student fixes the patterns and their order, until every visitor gets the right answer.

05:00.110 --> 05:01.326
The final quiz:

05:01.326 --> 05:04.568
events, regular expressions and intents.

05:13.277 --> 05:20.707
The last quest adds a chat window in the corner that answers with regular expressions and scrolls to the newest message.

05:28.443 --> 05:30.394
All five badges unlocked.

05:32.443 --> 05:35.946
And in the arena, the Glitch Overlord falls.

05:35.946 --> 05:37.697
Victory for the class!

05:59.977 --> 06:02.414
Everything you just saw ran live:

06:02.414 --> 06:06.624
real sign-in, real quizzes, and real GitHub verification.

06:06.624 --> 06:08.249
That's Glitch Academy.
